{
  "id": "Lyo.Recipe.Api",
  "name": "Lyo.Recipe.Api",
  "area": "Apps",
  "tagline": "HTTP mapping for the Lyo Recipe API (`BuildRecipeGroup`).",
  "description": "Maps Recipe Req/Res CRUD via `Lyo.Api` `CreateBuilder` (categories, ingredients, recipes, attachments) plus ingredient-line and step GET/PUT, nested notes/tags, and optional multipart upload when `IRecipeAttachmentFiles` is registered. Register with `AddRecipeApiFromConfiguration`, then call `BuildRecipeGroup`. Example host: `Lyo.Recipe.Api.Example`.",
  "features": [
    "`BuildRecipeGroup` maps Req/Res CRUD for categories, ingredients, recipes, and attachments.",
    "Ingredient lines and steps under `Recipe/Recipes/{id}/IngredientLines` and `…/Steps` (GET list, PUT replace, ids preserved). `GET/PUT/DELETE Recipe/Units` and `GET Recipe/Ingredients/{id}/Usage`.",
    "Nested `Notes` and `Tags` on categories, ingredients, and recipes; delete cascades those rows.",
    "`POST Recipe/Attachments/upload` accepts any file role (`Document`, `Scan`, `Card`, `Image`, `Other`) and returns 501 when the FileStorage helper is missing.",
    "`AddRecipeApiFromConfiguration` registers the Postgres store, Note/Tag stores on the same connection, and CRUD services."
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Map the Recipe API",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "services.AddLocalCache();\nservices.AddLyoQueryServices();\nservices.AddRecipeApiFromConfiguration(configuration);\nvar app = builder.Build();\napp.BuildRecipeGroup();"
    }
  ],
